// just enough of the Metal Shading Language standard library, in C++, to
// compile and run darktable's Metal kernel ports on the CPU. Used only by
// the emulator backend (dtcl_emu.cc); see dtcl.h.
//
// It is deliberately strict where Metal is: the vector math functions take
// arguments of one type, so a call mixing a scalar and a vector, which may
// not compile with Apple's compiler, fails here too.
//
// Two things differ from Metal and need the help of the build:
//  - clang's vector types have no constructor syntax, so float4(a, b, c, d)
//    is rewritten to make_float4(a, b, c, d) before compiling
//    (tools/metal/metal_kernels.py emu)
//  - unsuffixed floating constants are double in C++ and float in Metal,
//    so the emulator compiles with -fsingle-precision-constant

#pragma once

